  <title>Progress bars</title>
  <p>
    Orca can show progress-bar updates on your braille display so you can track tasks such as
    downloads or file transfers.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-progress-bars">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Progress Bars</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Braille updates</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca periodically shows progress-bar updates. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Frequency (secs):</gui> Sets the minimum
          number of seconds between updates for the same progress bar. Zero removes this minimum
          delay. Default: 10. Range: 0 to 100.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Applies to:</gui> Selects which progress
          bars provide updates. Choices: All, Application, Window.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>All</gui>: Progress bars in all
              applications.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Application (default)</gui>: Progress bars in
              the active application.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Window</gui>: Progress bars in the
              active window.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
